# tests/docker/arms.sha256 — the vintage arms, pinned to the bytes wordpress.org served.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The rehearsal cells that matter most (7a-7d) upgrade FROM versions that
# 70k live sites actually run, and the most faithful old arm is not something build-free.sh
# produces — it is the ZIP wp.org hands those sites. Two consequences follow. The bytes are not
# ours, so they must be pinned: an arm silently substituted (a re-rolled ZIP, a truncated
# download, a proxy's error page saved as a file) would make a cell green against code nobody
# runs. And the 4.8 line PREDATES `.distignore`, which build-free.sh hard-requires at the ref, so
# for those vintages there is no build path at all — the ZIP is the only arm that can exist.
#
# `resolve_arm_zip` (lib.sh) refuses any version absent from this file, and refuses to use a
# present ZIP whose digest disagrees. Adding a vintage means adding its line HERE, in the same
# commit as the cell that needs it; a downloaded-but-unpinned arm is exactly the failure mode.
#
# Fetched 2026-09-05 from https://downloads.wordpress.org/plugin/<file>. wp.org returns 200 for
# 4.7.9, 4.8.1-4.8.4, 4.8.7.3, 4.8.8, 4.8.8.1, 4.9.4, 5.0.10.2, 5.1.5, 5.2.13, 5.3.5, 5.4.12 and
# 5.5.0; only 4.8.0 and 4.8.8.2 are 404. Each file's plugin header Version was read after the
# download and equals the version in its name — which is the property the cell's H1 control
# re-asserts from inside the container, against what WordPress reports after installing it.
#
# Install share by bucket (wp.org API, read 2026-09-04): 5.5.x 41.1 %, 4.8.x 12.9 %,
# 5.2.x 11.1 %, 5.3.x 8.3 %, 5.4.x 7.5 %, "other" (4.9-5.1) 19.1 %.
#
#   sha256                                                            file
bab2b9e3287ce6c3fb8fc06240622a8225933f380f01897c4b61cb64554f2d47  wp-slimstat.4.8.1.zip
9e84cfc632730b228ce8e993a2bf2f79f9ece22aeda347f8e479f425766b9519  wp-slimstat.5.1.5.zip
63c91ad06c5708f0b0d5c163c52360d226742a7e529f3cd657332626b7a544d7  wp-slimstat.5.2.13.zip
